  "answer": "Retention view, April 2026: 61 customers are flagged as likely to leave, and 952 have already churned. The list below covers the 20 most valuable at-risk customers. Their combined spend over the last 12 months is \u20ac8,220.09.\n\n**Biggest names at risk (12-month spend)**\n- Anneli Sinkkonen, \u20ac803.60\n- Suvi Jokinen, \u20ac672.60\n- Antero Saarinen, \u20ac629.20\n- Suvi M\u00e4kel\u00e4, \u20ac616.43\n- Toivo Mattila (aquarium), \u20ac584.06\n\nTwo customers are rated \"very likely\" to leave: Raija Ojala (\u20ac420.27) and Laura Laitinen (\u20ac321.58).\n\n**What the view suggests**\n- Small-animal owners: an offer on PetNord Rabbit Pellets Food 12kg. Expected return is \u20ac7.29 to \u20ac12.74 per customer.\n- Aquarium owners: an offer on JBL Filter Pads. Expected return is \u20ac5.34 to \u20ac7.44 per customer.\n- Across all 20 customers, the best action is a personalised ad for 12, a \u20ac10 voucher for 3, an apology with \u20ac5 credit for 2, a 10% discount for 2, and a plain email for 1.\n- The 20 offers have an expected return of \u20ac202.76. The view puts the net gain of the best actions at \u20ac375.31, and each email costs \u20ac0.50. I can't explain why the net figure is higher than the expected return.\n\n**Proposed actions**\n1. Send the 12 personalised ads, starting with the rabbit-pellet customers (Retention view, `/retention/`).\n2. Contact the two \"very likely\" customers first, Raija Ojala and Laura Laitinen (Retention view).\n3. Send the \u20ac10 vouchers, the \u20ac5 credit apologies and the 10% discounts to the customers the view assigns them to (Retention view).",
